% Wall-Bang (enemy state machines)
%
% The Ram is a boss: heavy (nothing moves it) and immune to stuns. Its one
% move is a telegraphed charge down its lane: taunted or blinded, it lowers
% its horns and charges the brink - a heavy, PHYSICAL blow (nothing
% interrupts it). The team gets one cast; then the Ram lands on the brink,
% goring everyone there (stunned, and knocked wherever it throws them: into
% the rift, over the edge into the ravine, or nowhere). At the brink stands a
% stone pillar, and the charge ends in it:
%   taunted, blinded -> ramCharge: it dashes from the arena to the brink,
%                       gores whoever stands there, and crashes into the
%                       pillar: staggered, knocked off its feet (heavy no
%                       more)
%   staggered        -> the window: a knock or a hook drops it into the
%                       ravine; a vortex draws it into the rift
%
%   arena (Ram) ---- brink (pillar; the rift) ---- pen
%                      :                             |
%                      : (gap: the ravine)         gallery
%                      :                             |
%                     ledge -------------------------+
%
% Map: five areas. The brink and the ledge face each other across the
% ravine (a gap); the brink's lip is the rift (a chasm feature). The brink
% and the arena see each other; the pen, the ledge and the gallery see the
% brink; nothing else sees into the arena.
%
% The team splits: the player holds the brink, in front of the pillar; the
% mage waits in the pen. Whoever is still on the brink when the charge
% lands is gored (stunned: they finish nothing).
%
% Methods (the lure, then the finisher; the lure gets nothing to finish
% with, so it is never one companion's job):
%   flash and ...   blindingFlash in the arena: the Ram charges blind and
%                   leaves its caster behind
%   taunt and ...   taunt in the arena: it charges the brink all the same
%   ... finished by fireball from anywhere that sees the brink, tidalWave
%                   walking onto the brink after the charge, a vortex into
%                   the rift, a hook across the ravine from the ledge, a
%                   shield bash from next door
%   the brink holder finishes only if it survives the charge where it
%   stands, with one cast in the window: a shield bash at the Ram (the
%   shield takes the gore), or a hook at the heavy Ram (it drags its caster
%   into the arena, out of the way) - then round by the gallery to the
%   ledge, and hook the staggered Ram into the ravine
%
% Traps:
%   - a knock, a hook or a vortex before the crash does nothing (heavy);
%   - the charge is physical: a hook's or a bash's interrupt in the window
%     does not stop it;
%   - the brink holder with a fireball, a wave or a vortex is gored before
%     it can finish (a vortex on the rift in the window draws nobody away; a
%     fireball on itself throws it into the ravine);
%   - a hook from the pen only drags the staggered Ram onto the pen.

% === Areas ===
region(arena).
region(brink).
region(pen).
region(gallery).
region(ledge).
connected(arena, brink).
connected(brink, pen).
connected(pen, gallery).
connected(gallery, ledge).
gap(brink, ledge).
feature(brink, rift, chasm).
lineOfSight(arena, brink).
lineOfSight(brink, arena).
lineOfSight(pen, brink).
lineOfSight(brink, pen).
lineOfSight(ledge, brink).
lineOfSight(gallery, brink).
lineOfSight(pen, gallery).
lineOfSight(gallery, pen).
lineOfSight(gallery, ledge).
lineOfSight(ledge, gallery).

% === Companions ===
role(player, player).
role(mage, companion).
at(player, brink).
at(mage, pen).
mana(player, 4).
mana(mage, 4).

% === The Ram ===
role(ram, enemy).
at(ram, arena).
rank(ram, boss).
tag(ram, living).
tag(ram, heavy).

% Taunted or blinded, it charges its lane: heavy, physical. It dashes to the
% brink, gores everyone there (stunned, thrown), and crashes into the pillar
% (staggered, off its feet).
behavior(ram, taunted, ramCharge, there(brink)).
behavior(ram, blinded, ramCharge, there(brink)).
heavy(ramCharge).
effect(ramCharge, target, dash).
effect(ramCharge, self, grant(staggered)).
effect(ramCharge, self, remove(heavy)).
effect(ramCharge, target, grant(stunned)).
effect(ramCharge, target, push).

% === Default kit: one skill each (combos replans the whole matrix) ===
knows(player, blindingFlash).
knows(mage, fireball).

% === Victory ===
% Provoke the charge, see it crash, then the standard recipes finish the
% Ram in the state it is left in (a drop into the ravine or the rift).
win :- if(), do(provokeCharge(ram), confirmTag(ram, staggered), neutralize(ram)).

% Someone lands a tag it answers with its charge.
provokeCharge(?e) :-
    if(behavior(?e, ?t, ?ab, ?aim), heavy(?ab), canAct(?p), knows(?p, ?sk), grants(?sk, ?t)),
    do(cast(?p, ?sk, ?e)).

confirmTag(?e, ?t) :- if(tag(?e, ?t)), do().

funExpect(single_actor_plans, atMost, 0).
% The intent: every plan sets off the Ram's charge.
funIntended(opProvoked).

% === Choice: one skill each, from seven (htn_components combos) ===
comboSeat(player, 1).
comboSeat(mage, 1).
comboPool(blindingFlash).
comboPool(taunt).
comboPool(hook).
comboPool(vortex).
comboPool(fireball).
comboPool(tidalWave).
comboPool(shieldBash).
comboMinWins(8).
comboMinMethods(4).

goals(win).
